Dear group,

The recent thread pointing out the extra damage done by frost horns
used by monsters led me to peruse muse.c. It contains the following
defines:

 ...
 #define MUSE_WAN_DEATH 1
 #define MUSE_WAN_SLEEP 2
 #define MUSE_WAN_FIRE 3
 #define MUSE_WAN_COLD 4
 #define MUSE_WAN_LIGHTNING 5
 #define MUSE_WAN_MAGIC_MISSILE 6
 ...
 #define MUSE_SCR_EARTH 17
 ...

and the following code:

 ...
 #define nomore(x) if(m.has_offense==x) continue;
         for(obj=mtmp->minvent; obj; obj=obj->nobj) {
                 /* nomore(MUSE_WAN_DEATH); */
                 if (!reflection_skip) {
                     if(obj->otyp == WAN_DEATH && obj->spe > 0) {
                         m.offensive = obj;
                         m.has_offense = MUSE_WAN_DEATH;
                     }
                     nomore(MUSE_WAN_SLEEP);
                     if(obj->otyp == WAN_SLEEP && obj->spe > 0 && multi
>= 0) {
                         m.offensive = obj;
                         m.has_offense = MUSE_WAN_SLEEP;
                     }
                     nomore(MUSE_WAN_FIRE);
                     if(obj->otyp == WAN_FIRE && obj->spe > 0) {
                         m.offensive = obj;
                         m.has_offense = MUSE_WAN_FIRE;
                     }
                     nomore(MUSE_FIRE_HORN);
 ...

If I am reading correctly, this loops through all items in the
monster's inventory. It sets m.has_offense to 1 if the object is a wand
of death, then executes "nomore(MUSE_WAN_SLEEP);", which expands to
"if(m.has_offense==2) continue". As far as I can tell, at this point
m.has_offense is either 0 (if the item isn't a wand of death) or 1 (if
it is). So all cases are checked, and the monster ends up using the
weediest offensive item on the list.

I did a quick wizmode test by throwing a fire horn and a wand of death
to a soldier. It did indeed use the fire horn first.

So am I misreading the code, or is this a bug, or did the DevTeam
intend monsters to use their best items last?

Jason



